quickkey (1.4.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Keep retrying the daemon until a display exists.  A startx login reaches
    default.target minutes before X does, and the daemon cannot build its
    window without $DISPLAY, so it exited 1 and the old retry policy gave up
    after 20 seconds.  It now retries every 5s for ten minutes.
  * README: document that upgrading from a version before 1.0.1 leaves the
    enablement symlink in graphical-session.target.wants/, which on a startx
    session never activates, and that `systemctl --user is-enabled` reports
    `enabled` anyway.  `systemctl --user reenable quickkey` repoints it.

 -- ghollisjr <ghollisjr@gmail.com>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:50:00 -0500

quickkey (1.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Filter fuzzily: the query splits on whitespace and every term has to
    match somewhere in the name, in any order, so `pass 24` finds
    "Password (24 chars)".  A term matches a run of letters outright or as
    a subsequence, so `cb` finds "Current branch".
  * Ship a man page, quickkey(1).
  * Get off the screen before a background command starts, so a screenshot
    tool cannot photograph the picker.

 -- ghollisjr <ghollisjr@gmail.com>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 09:00:00 -0500

quickkey (1.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A command ending in & is launched and forgotten: no waiting, no output
    capture, no clipboard write, and the picker closes immediately.  Long
    lived programs such as libreoffice previously held the window open
    until they exited or the timeout fired.

 -- ghollisjr <ghollisjr@gmail.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0400

quickkey (1.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Place the picker on the monitor under the mouse pointer, instead of
    centring across the whole X display, which straddled the seam on a
    multi-monitor setup.
  * New --monitor option (active, primary, all).

 -- ghollisjr <ghollisjr@gmail.com>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:10:00 -0400

quickkey (1.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Write the PRIMARY selection as well as CLIPBOARD, so terminals that
    paste with Shift-Insert or middle-click see what was copied.
  * New --selection option (both, clipboard, primary).

